From d399654c01d4012ed951be6e8b970637507ef871 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "open-swe[bot]" <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 14:18:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/15] fix(hsm): bootrom reboot, lockout resync, fs-page
 guard, panic-reboot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-ups from the first validation campaigns (2026-08-02/03, all SWD-measured):

- chip_reset_now() uses the bootrom's rom_reboot(), not AIRCR.SYSRESETREQ:
  SYSRESETREQ resets only the asserting core on RP2040/RP2350 (raspberrypi/
  pico-feedback#329) and was measured as a complete no-op — RAM statics
  survived the write. rom_reboot is the field-proven path every UF2
  flash-update reboot takes.
- schedule_chip_reset(): a reset must never run inside an APDU handler —
  the response is transmitted after the handler returns, so a synchronous
  reset lands mid-command (host: Transmit failed). card_watchdog_task()
  fires the scheduled reset from core0's loop after the grace.
- Multicore lockout timeouts raised 1ms -> 100ms, and an end-timeout now
  re-syncs with a start+end pair: 1ms was far inside normal IRQ/entry
  latency, and a timed-out end orphaned core1 in the lockout victim
  handler forever (measured: core1 parked in multicore_lockout_handler,
  card mute).
- low_flash_task validates queued page addresses against the data region
  before touching flash: a corrupt entry (measured: address 0x20001A00,
  an SRAM pointer, after interrupted wipes) hit hard_assert(flash_offs +
  count <= PICO_FLASH_SIZE_BYTES) and PANICKED the device for a day.
- hard_assertion_failure() overridden: panic -> rom_reboot instead of
  panic -> bkpt -> _exit. A catatonic smartcard needs a site visit;
  a rebooting one recovers itself.
---
 src/fs/low_flash.c | 40 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/main.c         | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/usb/usb.c      | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/usb/usb.h      |  1 +
 4 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fs/low_flash.c b/src/fs/low_flash.c
index bb5db7f..eafea46 100644
--- a/src/fs/low_flash.c
+++ b/src/fs/low_flash.c
@@ -149,10 +149,22 @@ void low_flash_task(void){
         if (locked_out == true && flash_available == true && ready_pages > 0) {
             //printf(" DO_FLASH AVAILABLE\n");
             for (int r = 0; r < TOTAL_FLASH_PAGES; r++) {
+                if (flash_pages[r].ready == true || flash_pages[r].erase == true) {
+                    uintptr_t a = flash_pages[r].address;
+                    uint32_t off = a - XIP_BASE;
+                    if (a < XIP_BASE || off < (FLASH_SIZE_BYTES >> 1) || off >= FLASH_SIZE_BYTES) {
+                        printf("ERROR: flash_pages[%d] has out-of-region address %p — dropping entry, NOT erasing\n",
+                               r, (void *) a);
+                        flash_pages[r].ready = false;
+                        flash_pages[r].erase = false;
+                        ready_pages--;
+                        continue;
+                    }
+                }
                 if (flash_pages[r].ready == true) {
 #if defined(PICO_PLATFORM) || defined(ESP_PLATFORM)
                     //printf("WRITTING %X\n",flash_pages[r].address-XIP_BASE);
-                    if (multicore_lockout_start_timeout_us(1000) == false) {
+                    if (multicore_lockout_start_timeout_us(100000) == false) {
                         printf("WARN: FLASH LOCKOUT START TIMEOUT\n");
                         continue;
                     }
@@ -161,8 +173,16 @@ void low_flash_task(void){
                     flash_range_erase(flash_pages[r].address - XIP_BASE, FLASH_SECTOR_SIZE);
                     flash_range_program(flash_pages[r].address - XIP_BASE, flash_pages[r].page, FLASH_SECTOR_SIZE);
                     restore_interrupts(ints);
-                    if (multicore_lockout_end_timeout_us(1000) == false) {
-                        printf("WARN: FLASH LOCKOUT END TIMEOUT\n");
+                    if (multicore_lockout_end_timeout_us(100000) == false) {
+                        /* A timed-out END can orphan core1 in the lockout victim handler
+                         * forever (measured 2026-08-02: core1 parked in
